<title>HONG KONG: H B Int'l year profit down 21.34 percent.</title>
<headline>H B Int'l year profit down 21.34 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended July 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   10.4	vs 13.7</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	 vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  2.44 gain vs 12.00 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    53.50     vs 68.01</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,286.79  vs 1,172.98</p>
<p>    Company name		 H B International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  December 24-31</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - H B International is a maker of telephones and answering machines.</p>
<p>The exceptional item represents the over-provision for the loss on stocks due to a fire which occurred at a leased factory warehouse in the China in prior year.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 2.5 cents (including interim dividend of 2.5 cents) vs 6.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
